   "text": "This is a rifamycin-type ansa macrolactam whose naphthoquinone core is fused to a phenoxazine. The benzo ring of the phenoxazine carries a 2-(azepan-1-yl)ethoxy group.\n\nReading the drawing region by region:\n- **Ansa chain:** the amide NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013C(CH3)=CH\u2013CH=CH diene is followed by the methyl-, hydroxyl-, OAc- and OMe-bearing stereocentres, and then the enol ether O\u2013CH=CH. The chain closes onto the quaternary ketal carbon.\n- **Furanone ring:** the quaternary carbon carries a methyl, the enol-ether oxygen, the ring oxygen and the lactone C=O.\n- **Aromatic core:** a methyl-substituted, hydroxylated benzene ring is fused to the quinone-type ring. That ring carries the NH, the C=O and the phenoxazine C\u2013O and C=N carbons.\n- **Phenoxazine benzo ring:** it bears the OCH2CH2\u2013azepane substituent.\n\nI did not derive the stereochemistry of the chain independently from the wedges. I copied it from the known rifamycin/rifampicin stereo-SMILES, which I recalled from memory, and I re-derived the quaternary-carbon chirality symbol for my atom ordering. The drawing matches that rifamycin series.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1/C=C/C=C(\\C(=O)NC2=C3Oc4cc(OCCN5CCCCCC5)ccc4N=C3c3c(C2=O)c(O)c(C)c2c3C(=O)[C@@](C)(O/C=C/[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]1O)C)O)C)OC(=O)C)C)OC)O2)/C"
